  "notes": "いい{加減|かげん} has contrasting meanings depending on context:\n\n**Negative sense (most common in casual speech):**\n- いい{加減|かげん}な + noun = sloppy, irresponsible\n- いい{加減|かげん}⟦に→に：00314_ni⟧⟦しろ→する：00392_suru⟧/⟦して→する：00392_suru⟧ = stop it, that's enough (expression of frustration)\n\n**Positive/neutral sense:**\n- いい{加減|かげん}⟦に→に：00314_ni⟧ = moderately, appropriately\n\nThe phrase いい{加減|かげん}⟦に→に：00314_ni⟧⟦しろ→する：00392_suru⟧！is a strong expression of annoyance, often used when someone's behavior has become intolerable.",
